# sapintegrationsuite_partner_string_parameter (Resource)

A string parameter is a named text value stored for one partner ID (Pid), for example a
receiver address or a document format. Integration flows read it at runtime with the Partner
Directory steps, so one flow can serve many partners. Partner Directory data is stored
unencrypted: never put passwords, tokens or keys into a string parameter; use
[`sapintegrationsuite_partner_user_credential_parameter`](partner_user_credential_parameter.md)
for credentials.

**Status:** supported. Backed by `StringParameters` of the Partner Directory API.

## Prerequisites

- An OAuth client with the role `AuthGroup_TenantPartnerDirectoryConfigurator`.
- A partner ID (Pid) chosen by you. It does not have to exist: SAP creates a Pid the first time
  an entry references it, and there is no resource for partners themselves.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the parameter under `partner_id` and `parameter_id`; SAP creates the Pid if it is new. |
| Read | Reads the value. A value changed in the UI or by another process shows as drift. |
| Update | A changed `value` is written in place. |
| Replacement | Changing `partner_id`, `parameter_id` or `runtime_location_id` creates a new parameter. |
| Delete | Deletes this parameter only. Other entries of the same Pid are not touched. |

